@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · dsh-workbench：Register the MCP servers a **workspace** declares in `.mcp.json` with DeepSeek
Harness — through Harness's own `mcp-client`, not a reimplementation.

```jsonc
// <workspace>/.mcp.json — the same file Claude Code, Codex, and others read
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "sage": { "command": "/Applications/SAGE.app/Contents/MacOS/sage-gui", "args": ["mcp"] },

@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · Why workspace-mcp exists：Upstream cannot take this as a patch: `deepseek-harness` states that it does not
accept external pull requests, and directs changes of this kind to the plugin
ecosystem. This is that plugin.

@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · Legacy stdio integration：Setting `sage: {}` on the plugin row mounts one
[SAGE](https://github.com/l33tdawg/sage) MCP server per workspace, so each
workspace signs as its own agent instead of sharing one brain across projects.

@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · Legacy stdio integration：```yaml
- id: workspace-mcp
  config:
    sage: {}
```

@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · Substitutions：`${workspaceFolder}` and `${workspaceRoot}` resolve to `root`; `${cwd}` resolves
to the entry's own `cwd` once set, otherwise `root`. A whole-value
`${env:NAME}` resolves to `env[NAME]`.

@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · `clientModule`：```yaml
- id: workspace-mcp
  config:
    clientModule: {!!js ctx.loader.import('@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client')}
```

@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · Development：Each package under `packages/` also has its own test command, for when only one
suite is in question. The
[uplift README](packages/dsh-uplift/README.md#tests) lists the bundle's suites;
the [evaluation guide](research/RELIABILITY-EVAL.md#fixed-regression-scenarios)
gives the focused verification, completion and continuity checks.

@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · Development：`tests/integration.test.ts` bootstraps the real tool registry and the real
`mcp-client`, writes a `.mcp.json`, and asserts the fixture's tool lands in the
registry — the tests exercise the actual client rather than a stand-in.

@l33tdawg/dsh-workspace-mcp README · has a .mcp.json:："$DSH_HOME/node_modules/.bin/dsh" --profile check --dump-config   # composes the row
"$DSH_HOME/node_modules/.bin/dsh" --profile check "any task"      # boots it
```
